  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: fcf7219bab7fe46a1ad266029b2fee19, type: 3}
  m_Name: Readme
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Readme
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  title: UI folder layout
  sections:
  - heading: HUD and Menus
    text: HUD and menus should mostly be UXML files. HUD is specifically for UI that
      displays on top of the player view, when the player can move. Menus are the
      rest, with buttons and such
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Framework
    text: Should be mostly C# files. They control the flow and logic of the visual
      UI elements. The UI framework should only control the UI, and plug itself into
      the events of other systems. For the UI to impact other systems, calls and
      dependencies should be wisely managed and contained, and not overflowing with
      dependencies to everything, everywhere.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: StyleSheets
    text: Should be mostly USS files. They control the appearance of the UI
    linkText: 
    url: 
  loadedLayout: 1
